  "notes": "The authored exterior includes the long curved embankment, gray reservoir face, divided crest road with painted curbs, six pale blue vaulted roof bays, concrete galleries, control tower, electrical apron and six recessed outlet faces. The dam follows the signed PMTiles outline and native approaches. The Earth viewer now gives the reservoir and the downstream Euphrates representative stages of 326.55 m and 316.64 m. The lower stage meets the outlet apron below the six blue powerhouse roofs. The paired stages represent exterior visualization estimates. The model datum follows the host reservoir elevation sample. Ground and water contact depend on the host supplying the retained Protomaps IDs and comparable terrain. The apron equipment, outlet recesses and embankment details follow visual estimates.",
